        "Process_Category": "LPBF Additive Manufacturing and Heat Treatment",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "The LPBF fabricated samples were produced on a Concept Laser M2 machine with the laser power of 300 W, the scanning speed of 1100 mm/s, the layer thickness of 50 μm and the hatch spacing of 100 μm. The strip scanning strategy was employed in the fabrication process and the new layer was rotated 67° in the scanning direction relative to the previously deposited layer. All fabrication processes were carried out in an argon atmosphere. The H230AM samples were heat treated in the muffle furnace at 1200℃ for 1 h, then air cooled to room temperature.",
          "simplified": "LPBF: Concept Laser M2, 300W, 1100mm/s, 50μm layer, 100μm hatch, 67° rotation, Ar atmosphere. Heat treatment: 1200°C/1h, air cooled."
