      "Microstructure_Info": {
        "Microstructure_Text": {
          "original": "The network segregation phases are completely dissolved in the H230AM after normal atmospheric heat treatment, and extensive precipitated phases with sizes of 166±18 nm are uniformly distributed in the matrix... According to the SAED pattern and EDS results, the precipitated phase in the H230AM is identified as ZrC carbide... The introduction of 1 wt% Zr element in H230 alloy transforms the carbides from M6C to ZrC in the heat-treated microstructure... The number densities of carbides in H230AM... was 1.71 μm⁻²... The plate-like Ni7Zr2 phase with an average size of about 300 nm, is precipitated within the grain interior... The average grain sizes of H230AM... after heat treatment was 10.9 μm.",
          "simplified": "ZrC carbide (166±18nm, 1.71 μm⁻² density) uniformly distributed. Plate-like Ni7Zr2 phase (~300nm) within grains. Average grain size 10.9 μm."
        },
